  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` passes (5 tests, including 3 new regression tests).\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected job never decremented `running` or started the next job, so the queue stalled. Failures now release their slot and the queue moves on. A job that throws synchronously, or returns a plain value, is also handled, as the contract requires.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving early:** it only checked that nothing was pending. It now also waits until nothing is running.\n- **One job at a time after `resume()`:** `next()` started at most one job per call. It now loops until every free slot is filled, so `resume()` with concurrency 4 starts up to four jobs.\n\nThe new tests in `test/queue.test.js` cover failing and throwing jobs, `onIdle()` waiting for running jobs, and `resume()` filling all slots.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
